But the moment everyone is waiting for comes Tuesday morning, when Steve Jobs makes his annual keynote address at San Francisco¡¯s Moscone Center.
What can Jobs do to top that?
Nobody has yet shouted out ¡°Bingo! ¡± in middle of a Steve Jobs presentation &#8212;
a moment brilliantly anticipated in IBM¡¯s buzzword Bingo TV ad (link) &#8212; but this could be the year.
A Skinny MacBook.
Macbook air, thin, nano and mini &#8212;
LED backlit screen, under 3 lbs., half as thick as today¡¯s MacBooks, 32, 64 or even 128GB solid-state flash drive, priced around $1,600.
