Debt to a degree is healthy.
Triesman also called for a review of the "fit and proper persons" test that determines who may own English clubs.
"You get people turning up with banker's guarantees who are not interested in football and then they lose interest in the clubs and leave.
What happens to the clubs then?
" Blatter was quoted in The Times on Tuesday.
You have to prove your link with the area," he later told BBC Sport.
