De Niro lampoons Hollywood in new comedy
If you were looking for someone to write a pithy satire dishing the dirt on the highs and lows of Hollywood, then A-list producer Art Linson would be a pretty good bet.
He's got 25 years working with Tinseltown's finest under his belt, and his film credits include "Into The Wild" and "Fight Club."
Now he's turned his hand to writing.
First, a memoir detailing his experiences as a Hollywood producer, "Bitter Hollywood Tales From the Front Line."
And lately, adapting the book into a screenplay for the film, "What Just Happened," starring another Hollywood veteran, Robert De Niro.
The film, which is directed by Barry Levinson, tells the story of two weeks in the life of a nail-biting middle-aged Hollywood producer who is desperately trying to balance a set of outrageous crises in his day job with an equally complicated private life.
The film also features celebrity guest stars like Sean Penn and Bruce Willis mercilessly sending themselves up
