Terry sent off as Chelsea draw at Everton
England captain John Terry was sent off for a late tackle in the first-half, as 10-man Chelsea drew 0-0 at Everton, losing their 100 per cent Premier League away record in the process.
A win would have put Chelsea top of the table, but Liverpool retain that position, one point ahead of the London side.
The result means none of the so-called Premier League 'big four' have won for the second week in a row
and for the third time this season.
