Chinese hopeful Liu will return for Berlin
Former Olympic 110 meters hurdles champion Liu Xiang could return from injury in time to meet arch-rival Dayron Robles at the 2009 world championships in Berlin.
The 25-year-old was expected to be one of the faces of this year's Beijing Games but limped away from the Bird's Nest Stadium starting line due to an Achilles injury which was operated on earlier this month, ruling him out for six months.
But a leading Chinese athletics official believes Liu could be fit to defend his title in a battle with Olympic champion Robles of Cuba in the German capital in August, although he stressed Liu will not be pushed to make a return before he is ready.
Feng Shuyong, vice-director of the Chinese Athletics Administrative Centre, told the China Daily:
"If he can resume normal training in June, it's highly possible for him to participate in the world championships in August.
"But participating in the worlds is not a compulsory task for Liu.
