Meanwhile, against the Japanese yen, the greenback slid to ¥90.65 from ¥90.78.
"There's still a holiday feel in the air," said Nick Bennenbroek, head of currency strategy at Wells Fargo.
"The trading activity is very light, so the dollar is staying weak."
