Will the stock market rebound soon?
The roof caved in again today on the New York Stock Exchange, the Dow nose-diving 445 points.
But Al Goldman, Chief Market Strategist at Wachovia Securities, would not be surprised if the market rebounds tomorrow:
“The downward trend is still down, but if you want some good news, going by the climactic close, and the deeply oversold condition of the market, we do have the preconditions in place for at least a reflex oversold bouts.”
