Another month of record declines in house prices.
A closely watched index from Standard & Poor's shows the values of homes in twenty big cities plunged 18% in the year ending in October.
Those prices have been going down for nearly 2 years now.
In fact, the Case-Shiller Index shows houses are selling for about what they were back in 2004.
