An investigation into the work of discredited South Korean cloning scientist Hwang Woo-suk has found further fabrications in his research.
Dr Hwang's landmark claim to have cloned human embryonic stem cells was false, a university panel concluded.
But the panel, which last month rejected other research by Dr Hwang, has accepted that he did create the world's first cloned dog.
