An electric fault could have caused an overnight fire at the government building in downtown Seoul, which was put out within half an hour without causing any casualties, investigators said Thursday.
The blaze started in two adjacent rooms on the fifth floor of the 19-story Central Government Building just after 12:30 a.m.
Some 130 firefighters and 52 fire trucks were called to the scene and got the fire under control in about 30 minutes.
The 31 people in the building at the time of the fire fled to the rooftop and were able to leave safely after the heat and smoke subsided an hour later.
Electricity to the building was cut off to prevent the fire from starting again.
