The United States might have new direct consultations with North Korea during the current three-week recess in the six-party talks on ending the North's nuclear ambitions, top American negotiator Christopher Hill said.
Hill said he expected a flurry of bilateral diplomacy among all the parties before the fourth round of talks resumes on the week of August 29th in Beijing, where they recessed Sunday after 13 grueling days.
