PNG is in the grip of an HIV/Aids epidemic - the worst in the region.
Officials estimate that 2% of the six million population are infected.˝
The Joong-Ang Ilbo reports the Grand National Party broke an agreement and voted against a revision of tax law Friday.
Lawmakers from both the Uri and Grand National parties on the finance and legislative committees had agreed to approve the bill when, in a full session Friday, it failed to secure a majority, with only 107 yes votes out of a total of 222.
