The indigestion being felt on Wall Street is easing a bit as the Fed offer some main locks for investors.
“Stock prices opened higher but turned marginally lower in short order, as traders waited for developments from Washington and in the world economy.
Trading was light as investors waited reports of a new Federal Reserve scheme to break the log jam in the credit markets.
The latest idea would have the Fed hold billions of dollars in commercial paper, moving the central bank one step closer to lending directly to the private market but restarting the flow of day to day credit that nourishes businesses, both large and small. Warren Levinson, at the New York Stock Exchange.”
Yeah, and right now the Dow is down about 40 points.
