Witnesses said it was the worst fighting they had experienced in Gaza during 18 months of internal strife.
The Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency said Wednesday that it detected the organized school gang, ``Seoul Yonhap,'' comprised of 307 students from 29 smaller gangs in 94 schools and urged them to voluntarily disband.
The detection came amid a police crackdown on school gangs since last month.
Today’s Korea Times reports police have detected the largest-ever school gang in Seoul with its members consisting of more than 300 students from 94 middle and high schools.
The Seoul Metropolitan Police Agency said Wednesday that it detected the organized school gang, ``Seoul Yonhap,'' comprised of 307 students from 29 smaller gangs in 94 schools and urged them to voluntarily disband.
The detection came amid a police crackdown on school gangs since last month.
As violence and crimes among school gangs, well known as ``Iljinhoi,'' are getting worse, the government and law enforcement authorities have launched an intensive investigation and are encouraging gang members to voluntarily report to police.
