Ben Bernanke says the recession could end this year.
but only if the government can get financial markets to operate more normally again.
A new study indicates differences in health care by race continue right up until death.
Ezekiel Emanuel of the National Institutes of Health says dying blacks and Hispanics have much higher end care costs than whites:
“ Minorities seem to get more intervention, such as respirators, admission to the ICU, artificial feedings, at the end of life - when various studies have shown those interventions don't actually prolong life or improve the quality of life.”
