The BBC reports North Korea has tested a number of missiles in quick succession, one of which was a long-range weapon which failed seconds into flight.
The US said North Korea may have fired as many as six missiles.
At least three - two of them said to be shorter range - fell into the East Sea.
Both the US and Japan have acted with anger and dismay to the news.
US envoy to the UN, John Bolton, said he was ""urgently consulting"" with other Security Council members on the issue.
Both the US and Japan had said they would consider a range of options - including economic sanctions - if a launch of the Taeopdong-2 missile went ahead.
