The pain has persisted in the current quarter.
New claims for jobless benefits rose by 8,000 last week to 652,000, while continuing claims jumped to 5.56 million.
But despite the seemingly endless stream of dismal figures, there are some glimmers of hope.
Orders for costly manufactured goods and new home sales both logged unexpected gains in February.
Still, many analysts believe the economy will keep shrinking at least through the first six months of this year.
The government will release its initial estimate of first-quarter GDP in late April.
