Citing an official in Washington, the report said the U.S. government has begun a review of several North Korean accounts at the BDA following a recent Seoul government intelligence report that said the accounts appear to contain legitimate funds.
The official, speaking on the condition of anonymity, said it was not clear whether Washington's review was prompted by the report, but it may lead to unfreezing as much as half of North Korea's funds, or $12 million.
