Kim Jong-hoon, the chief South Korean negotiator in free trade talks with the United States, was promoted to the post of trade minister.
He replaces Kim Hyun-chong who was named to be ambassador to the United Nations in New York.
The pair helped hammer out a free trade agreement with Washington.
