The international community stepped up efforts over the Chuseok holiday to stop North Korea from testing a nuclear weapon, as concern grew that a test might be imminent.
The latest diplomatic efforts to dissuade the North from a test came yesterday, when Shinzo Abe, Japan's new prime minister, met President Hu Jintao of China.
Despite strained relations over Japan's imperial past and its interpretation of that history, the two leaders found common ground in discussing the North's nuclear brinkmanship.
Their meeting, China's Foreign Ministry told reporters, resulted in agreement on the issue that generally echoed a UN statement issued Friday.
The latest diplomatic efforts to dissuade the North from a test came yesterday, when Shinzo Abe, Japan's new prime minister, met President Hu Jintao of China.
