The Food and Drug Administration ordered an immediate recall of two species of farmed fish in markets here, less than a day after the Ministry of Maritime Affairs and Fisheries said that a carcinogen had been found at harmful levels in freshwater fish raised in captivity.
Late Wednesday night the Fisheries Ministry said it had discovered malachite green in carp and trout grown here.
The ministry said a check of 50 fish farms around the nation turned up traces of the chemical in fish from 34 sites.
