The Bank of Korea raised Korea's guiding interest rate by a quarter of a percentage point, to 3.5 percent, ending a period of record-low rates that began last November.
The Bank of Korea raised Korea's guiding interest rate by a quarter of a percentage point, to 3.5 percent, ending a period of record-low rates that began last November.
