North Korean leader Kim Jong-il visited the Chinese Embassy in Pyongyang over the weekend and received a personal message from Chinese President Hu Jintao, the (North) Korean Central News Agency reported.
The content of the message was not revealed.
South Korea and the United States have in principle agreed to exclude rice from their free trade agreement negotiations, The Korea Times quotes an official of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs as saying.
The provisional agreement was made during South Korean Trade Minister Kim Hyun-chong’s visit to Washington, the official said.
Rice is one of key sticky issues in the talks as farmers and civic groups have fiercely opposed the opening of the market.
In return, Seoul is expected to accept a U.S. demand that it fully opens its door to U.S. beef.
Meanwhile, the ministry officially criticized a group of U.S. lawmakers for urging their president to push Korea to abolish its 8-percent tariff on U.S. automobiles, saying such an attempt could wreck the talks.
