New York Governor Eliot Spitzer has resigned, after being linked to a prostitution ring.
Flanked by his wife, he told a news conference he could not allow ""private failings"" to disrupt public work.
He is to hand over power on Monday.
Spitzer again apologized for not living up to the standards he demanded of others - but he gave no details.
The governor had allegedly been identified arranging to meet a prostitute in a Washington hotel.
Spitzer made his name as an investigator of organized crime, financial crime and prostitution, and his fall from political grace is being seen as one of the biggest New York has known.
At one point he was known as the ""Sheriff of Wall Street"" for the vigor with which he pursued dirty dealing in high finance.
