Australia´s politicians have begun their general election campaigns, after prime minister John Howard set a 24th November date.
Howard pledged billions of dollars in tax cuts and launched a web video on climate change.
The opposition Labor Party has criticized Howard´s refusal to sign the emissions-limiting Kyoto agreement.
Howard is seeking a fifth term in office for his ruling Liberal-National coalition, but polls suggest a huge victory for Labor´s Kevin Rudd.
The 50-year-old opposition leader has been ahead of Howard in polls for most of the year.
Analysts say Howard has opted for a long election fight to give himself a chance of overhauling Labor´s lead.
