Korea's top officials yesterday ruled out the possibility of renegotiating the recently minted free trade agreement with the United States after Washington signaled dissatisfaction with labor and environmental issues.
””The United States may propose a renegotiation in the labor and environment sectors following consultations between the U.S. administration and Congress,”” Foreign Minister Song Min-soon told a parliamentary committee.
””But we made it clear during the talks that there will be no additional negotiations once the agreement is reached,”” Song told the National Assembly Committee on Unification, Foreign and Trade Affairs.
