The sanctions - being taken under a U.N.
Security Council resolution - will likely reduce the North Korean economy to a state worse than in the mid-1990s when millions died of hunger, the Korea Institute for International Economic Policy said.
The official exchange rate of the North Korean currency was 137 won to the U.S. dollar in the first half of 2005.
