Leaders from 21 Asian and Pacific Rim countries called for an early dismantlement of North Korea’s nuclear program at an international forum in Hanoi on Sunday.
In a chairman’s statement they adopted at the end of the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) summit, they expressed ”strong concerns ” about Pyongyang’s nuclear test on Oct.
9, saying it poses ”a clear threat ” to the goal of a nuclear-free Korean Peninsula.
