that, despite fresh economic news that would make the Grinch smile with glee.
The AP's Rita Foley is live in Washington to tell us about it:
“The bad news, Jon, covers joblessness and consumer spending.
The Commerce Department says spending fell six tenths of a percent last month.
And consumer spending does drive much of the economy.
As for unemployment, the Labor Department reports another 586,000 Americans signed up for jobless benefits last week.
