ietnam's leaders have decided to remove dozens of companies from the control of the armed forces and the ruling Communist Party.
Many state and party organizations have made large amounts of money by going into business.
Vietnam's armed forces own a mobile phone company, a bank, shipbuilders, textile factories and even hotels - in total more than 100 firms.
Most of these began by making weapons or uniforms but increasingly they have taken on a life of their own.
The party and party-controlled organizations will also lose control of their businesses.
