Doctors said Abe was being treated for a stomach complaint probably caused by extreme exhaustion and stress.
Such hospitalizations are common among failed political or business leaders in the country.
Japan´s governing party has announced it will choose a successor to Abe on September 23rd.
Finance Minister Fukushiro Nukaga has said he will stand, but the most likely candidate, former Foreign Minister Taro Aso, has yet to make an announcement.
