Police have named a student who shot dead at least 30 people at Virginia Tech university on Monday as Cho Seung-hui, a 23-year-old South Korean.
Cho was studying English and had been living on the university campus.
He killed himself after the rampage.
He is also thought to have killed two people earlier in the day.
It was the worst gun massacre in US history.
Virginia Governor Tim Kaine on Tuesday pledged to immediately launch an independent review of the events.
