German Chancellor Angela Merkel will visit South Korea in July on the first leg of her trip to Northeast Asian countries, an official at the Korean-German Chamber of Commerce and Industry (KGCCI) said Monday.
A government source said Merkel is expected to meet with President Roh Moo-hyun during her stay in Seoul to discuss ways of promoting ties between the two countries, particularly economic cooperation on the occasion of the 25th anniversary of the KGCCI.
