Time is running out for the six-party talks to be resumed this month as Pyongyang has not yet publicly reacted to Washington's request for ``good-faith actions'' in dismantling its nuclear programs.
If Pyongyang does not officially announce its return to the negotiating table by next week, the possibility of reopening the multilateral dialogue within this year will become ``really slim,'' an official in Seoul said on Thursday.
