The Joong-Ang Ilbo reports the High Court in Busan gave the go-ahead yesterday for a tunnel to be built for Korea's bullet train, turning down an appeal from environmentalists who said the project would destroy the habitat of rare amphibians.
Although construction of the bullet train rail bed between Seoul and Busan started in 1992, its completion has been delayed because of fierce opposition from environmental activists.
The opponents argued that an Environment Ministry's survey in 2002 showed that the new railroad would be built over what are Korea's largest wetlands.
