Lone Star Funds' cancellation last week of its planned sale of Korea Exchange Bank to Kookmin Bank has triggered a renewed debate on whether the prosecution's probe into the U.S. private equity group is scaring away foreign investment.
Foreign investors and the media have expressed worries that the drawn-out probe by Korean prosecutors into Lone Star has the risk of dampening the country's efforts to attract foreign investors, who have been choosing more economically viable competitors such as India and China.
