Warlord Mujahid Dokubo-Asari, speaking to Reuters during a break in the talks with President Olusegun Obasanjo, repeated his warning to foreign oil workers to leave the region, which pumps almost all of Nigeria's 2.3 million barrels per day output, until a final deal was achieved.
