The International Association of Athletics Federation (IAAF) on Tuesday selected the South Korean city of Daegu as host for the 2011 World Championships.
The IAAF made the decision when it held its 25-member executive council meeting in Mombasa, Kenya.
Daegu's rival cities were Brisbane, a resort city in Australia, and Moscow, Russia.
Daegu will be the third Asian city to host the biennial championships after Japan's Tokyo in 1991 and Osaka this year.
