The petrochemical industry is forecast to see domestic demand slip 0.8 percent.
The textile, steel and petrochemical industries are forecast to see a downturn in the second half of this year, and sluggish demand, the Korea Chamber of Commerce and Industry said yesterday.
In a survey of major industrial sectors, the KCCI said low-priced Chinese textile goods will continue to erode the market share of Korean players in the coming months, while higher oil prices will also weigh down on their already-slim margins.
Steel and petrochemical businesses are also expected to have trouble bolstering their sales due largely to shrinking demand and a decline in export orders.
