The White House has approved the nomination of Kathleen Stephens, senior State Department adviser for East Asia and Pacific affairs, as the next ambassador to Seoul, sources here said Thursday.
The State Department had recommended Stephens as the sole candidate for the post, and the White House accepted it at the end of last year, according to the sources.
Her nomination, after it is formally announced, needs to be confirmed by the Senate Foreign Relations Committee.
Formerly principal deputy assistant secretary of state for East Asia and the Pacific, Stephens would be the first female ambassador to represent the U.S. in South Korea.
She was the internal political unit chief at the American Embassy in Seoul in 1984-1987.
She also served as deputy assistant secretary for European and Eurasian affairs.
She speaks fluent Korean as well as Chinese and Serbo-Croatian.
