Enraged with the illegal use of their programs, the 11 companies led by Microsoft that claim the rights to the intellectual property filed a class action lawsuit on May 25 against the nine illegal users.
The Korea Times reports police Wednesday booked 259 people from nine companies without arrest on charges of circulating illegally downloaded software on the Internet.
Last month, police found that nine small and medium companies have illegally copied software programs and used them in violation of copyrights.
