The Joong-Ang Ilbo reports capture, neuter and release will be the city government’s modus operandi next year in its effort to quell the growing numbers of cats roaming the city’s streets, the Seoul city government said yesterday.
As many as 30,000 cats wandered Seoul as of 2004, city officials estimated, and the number has been increasing.
The city captured 4,599 cats last year, up from 2,851 in 2004, most of which the city euthanized.
Animal rights activists have been demanding the city government stop cat euthanasia.
Under the city’s Trap-Neuter-Return, or TNR, project, a cat will be caught in a trap, neutered by veterinarians, then released where it was captured after three to seven days of recovery.
