n an action hard to fathom in developed societies, thousands of doctors from Seoul and Incheon closed their clinics and took to the streets to protest the government-led revision of an old medical law.
They warned the action could spread across the nation despite concerns about the danger, inconvenience and distress it would cause patients.
The Korea Medical Association said about 5,000 members in the two cities participated in the three-hour rally outside the Government Complex in Gwacheon demanding the government scrap the revision.
