More than a million people are thought to have died during the four years of Khmer Rouge rule between 1975-79.
Judges spent several hours interviewing Duch on Tuesday before formally filing charges against him.
Duch was not among the top level of Khmer Rouge leaders but he has become one of the most notorious members, according to reporters in Phnom Penh.
He ran S21, a notorious jail where a total of more than 17,000 men, women and children were thought to have been imprisoned, many of them brutally tortured.˝
