South Korea plans to quietly ask the United States to sell it four surveillance planes to watch North Korea, though Washington refused to sell them last year, fearing technology leaks, the Joong Ang Ilbo quotes a government official as saying yesterday.
Seoul will ask to purchase the unmanned aerial vehicle Global Hawk during the upcoming Security Policy Initiative talks the official said, on condition of anonymity.
The request will be made informally, rather than on the official agenda, the official said.
