A former CIA officer whose identity was leaked to the media is suing US Vice-President Dick Cheney.
Valerie Plame is suing Cheney, his ex-aide Lewis Libby and presidential adviser Karl Rove, saying they tried to destroy her career.
Plame's name appeared in the media in 2003 after her husband criticized the Bush government over Iraq.
A spokesman for Rove, Mark Corallo, said the allegations were ""utterly without merit"".
It was revealed last month that Rove would not be charged over the leak.
