The nation's top spy agency said it yesterday will investigate allegations its former agents carried out massive eavesdropping operations on conversations of politicians and business leaders in the 1990s.
One of the illegal recordings allegedly contains a conversation between Hong Seok-hyun, former chairman of the JoongAng Ilbo and now ambassdor to Washington, and a Samsung Group executive in 1997 on plans to support a presidential candidate.
The controversy erupted as MBC, a local broadcaster, was preparing to air some of the tapes, which would hugely affect political and business circles.
