Samsung Group has hit a roadblock in its move to transfer chairman Lee Kun-hee’s wealth to his only son Jae-yong, as a court Tuesday convicted two of the group’s executives for assisting in the wealth transfer through illicit bond deals a decade ago.
The ruling, the latest in a series of blows to the nation’s largest conglomerate, is paving the way for the prosecution to investigate the Lee Kun-hee family for various stock and other asset transactions among family members.
The ruling is expected to have immense implications for the ownership and governance structure of Samsung Group going forward.
