Korean male teenagers who smoke begin a couple of months before their 15th birthday, half a year earlier than they did three years ago.
Yonsei University's Graduate School of Public Health surveyed 4,000 middle school and high school students.
But the number of teen smokers has decreased.
In 1999, about a third of high school boys smoked, but that ratio dropped to just under 16 percent in last year's survey.
