The rebels kidnapped 23 Christian charity workers from Ghazni province on 19 July.
They subsequently killed two male hostages, and freed two women.
The BBC´s Alastair Leithead, in Kabul, says no exact release date has been given, but the Taliban have said they will start working straight away to free them.
