A Taliban representative, an official from the South Korean government and mediators issued a statement in Ghazni - where the 19 are being held - saying that they had come to an agreement and the hostages would be released as soon as possible.
Meanwhile, the announcement was greeted with celebrations in South Korea, where families have been waiting anxiously for news of their loved ones.
The Christian church that the hostages belonged to, near Seoul, said all the families were ”rejoicing”.
