Mentioning his campaign pledge to make the country one of the world´s seven biggest economies, Lee said the goal is not ``pie in the sky´´ despite evidence to the contrary.
He cited two examples ― the Chinese government´s encouragement of people to have a competitive mind set against the United States and Japan´s full-fledged reshuffle of its government structure.
