The benchmark KOSPI closed down 65.22 points, or 3.85 percent, at 1627.19, while the tech-heavy Kosdaq market shed 19.26 points, or 2.95 percent, finishing at 634.52.
Analysts say the fall comes in line with global equity losses and concerns of a U.S. economic recession.
