A series of court rulings have determined that parents are partially responsible for car accidents involving their unattended children.
The Seoul Central District Court ruled Sunday that the insurance company was 50 percent liable for the accident and must pay the parents 90 million won in compensation.
The court said that the parents were also liable, because they had let their child play unattended at night on a busy road.
