The Supreme Court yesterday disclosed the finalized details of the new registration law, promulgated last month to replace the hoju system beginning in 2008.
Under the revised family registration law, each family member will be separated from hoju - the head of the family and usually the father - through an individual register book.
Children will no longer be obliged to go by the father’s surname and can follow the mother’s.
