The Bank of Korea kept its benchmark interest rate frozen for a sixth consecutive month yesterday as the central bank's governor, Park Seung, softened his optimistic view of the economy.
Speaking at a news conference, Park said that domestic consumption is picking up but the rebound is not strong enough to compensate for slowing exports, the sole growth engine the past two years.
