Seoul's proposal for a peace regime is expected to include a peace treaty, which will replace the armistice signed at the end of the 1950-1953 Korean War.
The two Koreas remain technically at war although they signed a nonaggression treaty in 1992.
Experts say Seoul hopes the two Koreas will take the lead in forming a peace mechanism.
