Five Korean workers and a local employee were abducted by gunmen in the Niger Delta of southern Nigeria 0, the Foreign Ministry said yesterday.
The Korea Herald reports the Korean workers, three employees of Daewoo Engineering and Construction Corp.
and one each from Korea Gas Safety Corporation and Korea Gas Technology Corporation, were kidnapped in an oil field in Port Harcourt.
The militia, identified as the Movement for the Emancipation of the Niger Delta, later indicated it was willing to release the hostages in exchange for the freeing of Asari, the leader of the illegal Niger Delta People's Volunteer Force.
Asari was arrested in September last year and is standing trial for treason.
