EU Trade Commissioner Peter Mandelson and South Korean trade minister Kim Hyun-Chong both called for rapid progress in free trade negotiations.
Kim said it was a chance to become East Asia’s free trade hub linking Europe, Asia and the US.
The first talks, from 7 to 11 May, will take place in Seoul.
Officials hope to conclude negotiations within a year.
In a joint statement the two ministers said a free trade agreement (FTA) would “open new markets and expand opportunities for Korean and EU businesses while giving valuable momentum to liberalization of global trade”.
˝Three men have been arrested in Germany on suspicion of planning a “massive” attack on US facilities in the country, officials have said.
Federal prosecutor Monika Harms said the three had trained at camps in Pakistan and procured some 700kg (1,500lbs) of chemicals for explosives.
She said the accused had sought to target facilities visited by Americans, such as nightclubs, pubs or airports.
Defense Minister Franz Josef Jung said the men had posed ”an imminent threat”.
Media reports said the men were planning attacks against a US military base in Ramstein and Frankfurt airport.
The US praised the actions of the German government and said the incident showed everyone needed to be vigilant in finding ”terrorists”.
