Moroccans Jamal Zougam and Otman el Ghanoui were convicted of murder along with Emilio Trashorras, a Spaniard.
But suspected ringleader Rabei Osman was cleared over the March 11th 2004 blasts on four trains that killed 191 people and injured more than 1,800.
