The violence broke out after anti-U.S. demonstrators broke through riot police lines late Friday afternoon to try to cut down the fences.
The Defense Ministry said before the clash that it had ordered the troops not to use force against protesters under any circumstances.
They were to have been protected by a cordon of riot police, armed with batons and shields... the police, however, themselves demoralized after being accused of causing the deaths of two farmers during violent protests in Seoul last November, and were unable to keep the protesters away from the troops.
