As the Bush administration faces the November presidential election the United States claims it and its allies have put Osama bin Laden on the defensive, increasing chances of his capture soon, according to remarks published in Pakistani media on Sunday.
Cofer Black, State Department coordinator for counter-terrorism, said in Islamabad the entire ""infrastructure"" was in place to capture bin Laden and his close lieutenants, Pakistan's English language Daily Times reported.
