General Assembly on Monday delayed a vote on a resolution urging compliance with a world court ruling that Israel's security barrier in the West Bank was illegal and should be torn down.
The Palestinians had sought a vote in the 191-member assembly urging Israel to obey the July 9th court opinion, but European Union states sought to include mention of the Middle East peace process in the resolution, a European diplomat said.
