A senior Russian government official said yesterday that the United States has rejected a request for political asylum from a North Korean man who sought refuge at the U.S. consulate in Vladivostok.
The man, who has not been named, entered the U.S. consulate on Oct.
26, in what is believed to be the first time a North Korean has asked for asylum at a foreign mission in Russia.
The official said the North Korean had worked as a logger in Russia.
