“ This morning, visibility was zero.
You could not see your hand in front of your face this morning out there.
” The county's Public Safety Director, Paul Whitten, says they're not giving up:
“ For us, in the unincorporated portion of Horry County, this fire is not done, and we're fully involved in fighting this, and we've got several more days to go.”
The fire is burning across the Intracoastal Waterway from Myrtle Beach itself.
