The North Korean Army announced yesterday that it would ""re-examine"" the armistice agreement that suspended the Korean War and agreements between Pyeongyang and the United Nations Command.
The announcement said, with probably intended irony, that the United States would no longer be fulfilling its responsibility under the armistice if it withdrew its troops from the Joint Security Area, the small border enclave that includes Panmunjeom.
Last July, Seoul and Washington reached an agreement to transfer the partial U.S. responsibility for guarding the security area to South Korean troops.
