Desperate to rescue his negative image in the field of diplomacy and foreign relations in the last year of his tenure, US President George W Bush has said he is prepared to exert pressure so that Middle Eastern peace talks can succeed.
“If there needs to be a little pressure then you know I will provide it,” he said after talks with Israeli prime minister Ehud Olmert.
He was speaking at the start of what he called an ”historic” tour of the Middle East aimed at advancing peace talks.
However, within hours of his arrival, the Palestinians reported that Israeli forces had killed three people in Gaza.
