The ripple effect of Bear Stearns´ liquidity trouble stemming from subprime-linked defaults continued and rattled Asian bourses, from Hong Kong, Singapore to Shanghai and Japan.
As Bear Stearns faced a near collapse, the New York Federal Reserve quickly moved to bail out the fifth largest investment bank on Wall Street through JPMorgan Chase.
