7, struck off the town of Pangandaran at 3:19 local time, causing a 2m-high wave.
One resident said high waves had destroyed hotels in Pangandaran and thrown boats onto the beach.
A Red Cross official in the area, said 105 people were believed to have been killed, with 148 injured and 127 still missing.
