Partial results put Mitt Romney and John McCain neck and neck in Florida, a key battle for Republicans seeking to run for president in November.
With votes still being counted, former New York Mayor Rudy Giuliani - who has staked his bid for the party nomination on Florida - was trailing in third.
Former Arkansas Governor Mike Huckabee, who also pinned his hopes on Florida, was fourth, with 11% of votes counted.
