The prosecution said it will appeal to the Supreme Court on Friday, and later to the Constitutional Court, to review the court's refusal to approve the arrest of the head of Lone Star's Seoul office on stock manipulation and tax evasion charges.
”The prosecution will appeal to the top court on Friday after reviewing the reasons for the Seoul Central District Court's rejection, ” prosecutor Chae Dong-wook told reporters.
