Secretary General Kofi Annan on Sunday arrived in South Korea, on the first leg of his Asian tour that will also take him to Japan, China, Vietnam and Thailand.
He plans to hold a meeting on Monday with Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Ban Ki-moon, a candidate seeking to become the next U.N. leader when Annan's second five-year term ends on Dec.
