The prosecution yesterday arrested a Korean-American businessman at the center of a wiretapping and slush fund scandal involving Samsung Group and high-profile politicians.
William Park, who is 58, is suspected of leaking an illegally bugged conversation that took place in 1997 between a Samsung executive and Hong Seok-hyun, Korea's ambassador to Washington, discussing plans to provide illegal campaign funds to presidential candidates.
After failing to make a deal with Samsung, he provided the tape to a reporter at MBC-TV, a local broadcaster, which aired the content last week.
