More than four in five multinational foreign executives in Korea said they wouldn't consider setting up regional headquarters in Korea for a wide range of reasons including labor inflexibility, language barriers and a number of other factors including cost of living.
The labor environment topped their list of concerns with only 18.6 percent saying it was OK.
The negative response comes in light of series of strikes at POSCO, Hyundai Motor and other leading conglomerates.
