”Japan should take substantive actions to resolve the issues surrounding Dokdo, history textbooks, visits to the Yasukuni Shrine and military sex slaves during World War II, ” he said in a televised speech during a ceremony to mark Korea’s 61st anniversary of Liberation Day from Japanese colonial rule.
