as part of economic cooperation projects agreed upon in their leaders´ recent summit.
Yonhap News Agency quoted an unnamed Unification Ministry official as saying that Seoul proposed December 11th as the date to start the railway service through the demilitarized zone, but that North Korea´s response was not yet known.
The agreement to open the railway service came on the second day of talks between South Korean Prime Minister Han Duck-soo and North Korean Premier Kim Yong-il in Seoul.
The rare prime ministerial talks were aimed at devising concrete plans to implement wide-ranging accords reached between the leaders of the Koreas.
